I remember when some web search engines were case-sensitive.
There are good reasons they're not anymore.  It does create some
difficulties in a handful of exotic situations (e.g., somebody talks
about an organization called the NOW and I want to search for
it to find out what it is), but in the overwhelming majority of cases
it's an improvement.  Plus, as you say, there are sites where
you can look up acronyms specifically.

Categorically ignoring all diacritical marks is also correct
behavior for a web search engine, in my considered opinion.
Trying to support them causes more problems than it solves.


